Welcome!

> My question is what information is considered a spoiler?  I've been 
> trying to play using mostly just information from the beginner's guide. 

I would say that spoiler information is anything that spoils the game's 
surprises for you and takes away the possibility for you to discover 
things in the game yourself.
While I would say the information in guides, like the beginner's guide, 
is spoilish, there is a difference in degree to the spoilers that 
explain some aspect of the game in extreme detail.
After all, it is you yourself who decide what will make the game most 
enjoyable to you, and it is not so much a question of 'spoiled' or 'non-
spoiled' but deciding what level of spoiledness suits you best.
A very extreme stance on spoilers would be to (try to) not use anything 
outside the current game's/character's knowledge. Even if you knew since 
your last game that a scroll you can sell for a certain price has 
certain properties, you would not use this knowledge. Very extreme.
A still extreme but more realistic approach would be to not use anything 
outside 'normal games', which would mean no 'wizmode' testing, no asking 
for general strategy tips on RGRN, etc.

>   I've read a couple posts on rgrn but for the most part have been 
> trying to figure everything out for myself.  I'm wondering though if 
> most people figure out how everything in the game works through trial 
> and error.

(It's hard to say anything about all the lonely Nethack players out 
there, who might be avoiding any contact with other humans. What I can 
say something about is the players who are posting in RGRN and obviously 
other players I know IRL.)
Extremely few people play Nethack without ever reading a spoiler, 
strategy guide, or getting spoilish tips from other players.
There are those who manage to play virtually unspoiled - and I think we 
all somehow look up to them and envy their patience, cunning and game 
immersion, at least I do. (For an entertaing *long* story by an 
unspoiled player, see here: 
<http://roguelikes.sauceforge.net/pub/nethack/stories/> *Warning, 
contains spoilers!*)
Many people who post in RGRN know most of the spoilers by heart, partly 
from reading them and partly from long experience in playing. One 
personal attitude towards spoilers can be that it is OK to look up 
things in spoilers between games, but when currently playing a game not 
allowing oneself to use any knowledge that has to be looked up.

/Kristoffer (Nethack, very spoiled. Slash'em, mostly unspoiled except 
for experience.)

